    "q-111104": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111104",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-2k+2 \\\\ 4k-4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2k+2=0 \\\\ 4k-4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
